From: lavachemist <48248311+lavachemist@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: edt-ft5x06 - release contacts the controller stops reporting, on the AYN Thor

The driver releases a slot only when the controller sends TOUCH_EVENT_UP
for it. When that one report is lost, the contact stays down for good.
On the AYN Thor's bottom screen (FT5452) this left two contacts frozen at
fixed positions with no finger on the panel, so every touch afterwards
looked like part of an old multi-finger gesture: the Barry Launcher
trackpad only scrolled and never saw the pad go idle.

The controller lists every current contact in each report, so on
"ayn,thor" let the input core drop the slots a frame leaves out
(INPUT_MT_DROP_UNUSED with input_mt_sync_frame()). Frames that fail to
read still report nothing. The flag lives in input->mt, so the patch adds
no state and leaves the kernel's BTF, and so the modules built against
it, unchanged. Other boards using the driver (the Retroid
Pocket 6 among them) keep the old behaviour.

--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/edt-ft5x06.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/edt-ft5x06.c
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 #include <linux/irq.h>
 #include <linux/kernel.h>
 #include <linux/module.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
 #include <linux/property.h>
 #include <linux/ratelimit.h>
 #include <linux/regmap.h>
@@ -377,6 +378,13 @@
 					       x, y, true);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * A contact the controller no longer lists has lifted, even if its
+	 * TOUCH_EVENT_UP never arrived: release it rather than leave it down
+	 * for good. Frames that failed to read skip this (goto out above).
+	 */
+	if (tsdata->input->mt->flags & INPUT_MT_DROP_UNUSED)
+		input_mt_sync_frame(tsdata->input);
 	input_mt_report_pointer_emulation(tsdata->input, true);
 	input_sync(tsdata->input);
 
@@ -1344,8 +1352,15 @@
 
 	touchscreen_parse_properties(input, true, &tsdata->prop);
 
+	/*
+	 * Only the AYN Thor is known to lose TOUCH_EVENT_UP reports. No new
+	 * state here: the flag lives in input->mt, so the kernel's BTF (and
+	 * with it the modules built against it) stays the same.
+	 */
 	error = input_mt_init_slots(input, tsdata->max_support_points,
-				    INPUT_MT_DIRECT);
+				    INPUT_MT_DIRECT |
+				    (of_machine_is_compatible("ayn,thor") ?
+				     INPUT_MT_DROP_UNUSED : 0));
 	if (error) {
 		dev_err(&client->dev, "Unable to init MT slots.\n");
 		return error;
